# Correlate by assignment with the two-model filter and sensor bias estimation.
# As correlate-assign-imm, plus one position offset per pair of sources. Before
# an estimate exists, a track of one source is compared with another source's
# tracks with 300 m added to the uncertainty on each axis, so a sensor offset
# by a few hundred meters still joins. Each tick, every pair of members of one
# system track from two sources refines the offset: an inverse-variance
# weighted mean, accepted while the pair's residual stays below gate = 13.82
# (chi-square 2 degrees of freedom, 0.1 %). The added uncertainty falls as
# 300² / (pairs + 1), to no less than 10 m.
pack        correlate-assign-bias
version     0.1.0
method      assign
filter      accel_var=1 default_ce_m=50 vel_sigma_ms=5 unknown_vel_ms=100
maneuver    accel_var=400 p_enter=0.05 p_leave=0.1
gate        mahalanobis gate=18.42
gate        same key=track.simulated
gate        same key=@env
new_cost    9.21
keep_bonus  2
stale_ms    120000
bias        sigma_m=300 floor_m=10 gate=13.82
